  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Tow your physically articulated trailer across the suspended course. Movement
    controls steer/throttle/brake; hold ACTION for the trailer brake. Crosswind affects
    the actual load. Fastest Crossing ranks successful crossings by elapsed time.
    Precision Hauling rewards preserved cargo and staying near the roadway center,
    with measured deviation and jackknife penalties; speed is not its judging criterion.
    Survival Highwire ranks actual time alive, including when every competitor eventually
    falls. Technical Jackknife rewards controlled articulated gate passages and requires
    actual reverse travel in the marked elevated backing section. Precision and Technical
    variants use their marked alternate elevated roads. Stop signs require both real
    bodies to settle; the Technical backing sign requires actual reverse motion of
    tractor and trailer. Moving crossing gates are real obstacles: wait for GO and
    let the entire load clear. Pass gates in order. A fall or lost hitch ends your
    attempt; no invisible safety floor supports the trailer.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
